    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42128" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sābrăta</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sābrătha</span></b> ),
			ae, f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a town of Africa</i>, <i>near the Lesser Syrtis</i>, now <i>Sabart</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				5, 4, 3, § 25</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sol.
			27</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sābrătensis</span></b> , e,
				adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Sabrata</i>, <i><span class="en">Suet.
				Vesp. 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cypr. Conc. Carth. p.
			120</span></i>.</div>
